WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.535
-Let's get to the news
and jokes.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.837
Well, guys, today,
President Trump took a break

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:08.307
from his busy schedule
of retweeting Randy Quaid

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:12.445
and carried out the presidential
tradition of pardoning a turkey.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.483
Here's the big moment between
Trump and a turkey named Corn.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:21.788 line:0%
-Corn, I hereby grant you
a full pardon.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.089 line:0%
Thank you, Corn.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.025
-Yeah. That's right.
The bird needed to be pardoned

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.194
after it was let down
by its bumbling lawyer,

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.829
Rooster Giuliani.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.332
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.367
[ Applause ]

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.335
Yeah, the good news is,
the turkey was pardoned.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:38.504
The bad news is,
Trump didn't wear a mask,

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.240
so he's a goner anyway.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.176
But I hope everyone else
wore a mask,

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.610
'cause it's gotta be
embarrassing

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.814
if your contact tracing
leads back to a turkey pardon.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.848
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:51.384
I saw that people
could go online

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:56.055
and vote for the turkey they
wanted pardoned, Corn or Cob.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.224
Meanwhile, it turns out
Corn might've won

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.627
'cause the vote was rigged
by Hugo Chavez.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.428
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.697
But this is nice. I heard
that before the ceremony,

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.333
Corn and Cob stayed
at the Willard Hotel.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.636
Take a look at this.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.639
Yeah. As if the hotel industry
wasn't going through enough

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.640
during COVID, now they
got to deal with this --

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.309
two turkeys in a suite.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.877
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.946
Yeah, while you've been stuck
in your studio apartment

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.114
for nine months,

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.215
Corn and Cob have been
demolishing the mini bar

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:25.552
and renting movies
at the Willard Hotel.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:26.953
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.422
That's right, the turkeys
have been staying at the hotel,

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.624
although it was sad
when they saw a feather pillow

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.726
and yelled,
"Look what they did to Steve."

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.195
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.529
Some more news
about the president.

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:39.799
I heard that he's planning
to move to Florida,

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.601
and a certain group people
are being asked

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.736
if they might want to go
with him. Watch this.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.339 line:0%
-Members of the president's
Secret Service detail

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:49.208 line:0%
have gotten an offer from
the Secret Service headquarters

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:52.344 line:0%
asking if they would like to be
permanently moved to Mar-A-Lago

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:55.882 line:0%
with the soon-to-be
ex-president Donald Trump.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:58.651
-Yep. When Trump asked who wants
to go to Florida with him,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.386
the agents broke
the Guinness World Record

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.789
for the longest silence
in history.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.892
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:09.495
Seriously, imagine going
from protecting the White House

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:14.300
to "The omelet bar is secure."

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.371
Repeat, the omelet bar
is secure."

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.406
Meanwhile, down at Mar-A-Lago,
I read that they're already

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:23.042
renovating Trump and Melania's
living quarters.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.510
This is nice.
To make Trump feel better,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.013
they're redoing every room
to look like the White House.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.348
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.584
Trump's actually getting
the work done at a good price

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.552
'cause they're going to grab
all the unused lumber

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.321
from the border wall.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.457
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.925
[ Applause ]

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.460
So congrats to the Trumps

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.397
and whichever bank repossesses
that property.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.099
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.100
Oh, this is a big story.
President-Elect Biden

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.304
has started naming key members
of his cabinet. Check it out.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.673 line:0%
-President-Elect Joe Biden
beginning to build out

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.108 line:0%
his cabinet with a diverse group

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.944 line:0%
including Janet Yellen
for Treasury Secretary

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.580 line:0%
and former Secretary of State
John Kerry

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.118 line:0%
to serve as a special envoy
on the climate crisis.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.653
-Yeah, Janet Yellen
and John Kerry.

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.489
Whoa, baby, get pumped!

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.123
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.559
Meanwhile,
when I saw those people,

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.861
I was like, "Wait, none of them
have been on a game show?"

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:17.763
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.565
Looking at Biden's cabinet
versus Trump's

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:23.269
is basically like comparing the
White House to "Animal House."

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.204
Listen to this. Joe Biden
announced his picks

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.839
for his presidential cabinet
this week.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.474
And this is cool.
We actually got our hands

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.311
on the voicemails Biden left
for his cabinet members

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.745
telling them the good news.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.547
This first one
is for his Secretary of State,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.048
Antony Blinken. Take a listen.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:37.216 line:0%
[ Beep ]

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.784 line:0%
-What's up, Skip?
Just calling to let ya know

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:40.987 line:0%
you're gonna be
my Secretary of State.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:44.089 line:0%
Hey, remember the days when
you could marry the secretary?

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:47.226 line:0%
You'd go, "Hey, missy. I have an
appointment to see the boss man,

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.028 line:0%
but now I'm wondering
if I could take you

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.030 line:0%
to the egg cream stand."

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.131 line:0%
[ Click ]

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:55.401 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.003 line:0%
-This next voicemail is for
Secretary of Homeland Security,

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.939 line:0%
Alejandro Mayorkas.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.807 line:0%
[ Beep ]
-Hey, Alejandro.

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:04.776 line:0%
I need you to keep our country
safe from the bad guys,

00:04:04.776 --> 00:04:08.013 line:0%
like teenyboppers who smash
your mailbox with a bat

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:09.815 line:0%
from the backseat
of a Winnebago,

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:13.052 line:0%
or Polish guys at the YMCA
who slap your back

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.954 line:0%
when you're wearing
a wet T-shirt.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.255 line:0%
[ Click ]

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:18.758 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:22.561 line:0%
-And finally, this voicemail is
for the new Treasury Secretary,

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.063
Janet Yellen.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.431 line:0%
[ Beep ]
-God, how many of these

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.700 line:0%
do I have left? Oh, I'm on.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.001 line:0%
Janet Yellen?

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:32.571 line:0%
You'd be responsible for
deciding which money is best.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:33.806 line:0%
I'm partial to the nickel

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.542 line:0%
'cause it's given us
so many classic games --

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.411 line:0%
Roll the Nickel Down the Hill.
Hop Over the Nickel.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.947 line:0%
Tease the Nickel.
Taste the Nickel.

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.649 line:0%
-This mailbox is now full.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.418 line:0%
Goodbye.
-Yeah, that's --

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:46.985
[ Applause ]

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:49.856
Hop Over the Nickel, that was
one of my favorite games.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.424
Some TV news. I saw
that "The Queen's Gambit"

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:55.828
just became the most-watched
scripted limited series

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.263
on Netflix.

00:04:58.263 --> 00:04:59.798
It's amazing. All it took

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:02.334
was closing every bar, gym,
and restaurant in America

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.704
to get people to care
about chess.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:09.075
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.542
And thanks to
"The Queen's Gambit,"

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.446
sales of chess sets are way up.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.548
Right now, elves
in Santa's workshop are like,

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.115
"Is this some kind of joke?

00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:20.286
What's -- Chess sets?"

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:23.255
The most popular games
are puzzles and chess,

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:26.626
so get ready for the hottest
Christmas of 1927.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.661
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.530
It'll be weird when kids
are like, "Is it a chess set?

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.433
Oh, it's just a PS5."

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:37.003
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:40.306
"Thanks, Santa."

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:43.075
It reminds me of when
"The Great British Baking Show"

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:44.409
debuted on Netflix,

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:47.713
and sales of type 2 diabetes
medication skyrocketed.

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.148
Reminds me of that.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:52.952
Get this. I heard that a lot
of Peloton customers are upset

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:56.122
because their orders have been
delayed for months.

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.590
Yep. Right now,
customers are like,

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.191
"How am I supposed to regret
buying this thing

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:00.793
if it never comes?"

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.529
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.464
You can tell
Peloton is getting desperate.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:06.832
Today they mailed people
a Schwinn

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.168
with a 9-inch TV
duct-taped to it.

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.437
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.405
Hey, guys, the news can
sometimes be pretty heavy.

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:16.208
So I thought I'd take a second
to focus, in a poetic way,

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:18.277
on some of the news stories
that you might have missed

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.611
that are a bit lighter.

00:06:19.611 --> 00:06:23.483
You'll see what I mean.
It's time for "In Lighter News."

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:27.386
-♪ In Lighter News ♪

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:28.654
[ applause ]

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:32.691
-Roses are red,
violets are symmetric.

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:34.693 line:0%
15 Philadelphia mobsters
indicted

00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:37.196 line:0%
including Tony Meatballs
and Joey Electric.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:39.832 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.969 line:0%
Roses are red,
violets are plants.

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:46.973 line:0%
Brawl at Colorado In-N-Out ends
with customer losing his pants.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.575 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:52.711 line:0%
Roses are red,
violets have grace.

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:57.149 line:0%
Martial artist removes 68 bottle
caps in 1 minute using his face.

00:06:57.149 --> 00:07:00.219 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.455 line:0%
Roses are red, violets are glum.

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:06.058 line:0%
Fed-up driver makes his son
stand in 6-foot pothole

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.427 line:0%
to prove how huge it's become.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:11.464 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:15.334 line:0%
And finally, roses are red,
violets are daft.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.702 line:0%
Two pilots under investigation

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:19.404 line:0%
for drawing gigantic penis
with aircraft.

00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:21.641 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:26.011
-♪ In Lighter News ♪

00:07:26.011 --> 00:07:28.513
And finally, here's some news
from overseas.

00:07:28.513 --> 00:07:34.186
Queen Elizabeth just launched
her own brand of gin.

00:07:34.186 --> 00:07:35.855
Yeah, I'm excited about this,

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:37.322
'cause I think
we're a month away

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:39.625
from the queen launching
her own line of vape pens.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:40.926
Guys, last night after our show,

00:07:40.926 --> 00:07:42.327
we all went down,
me and The Roots,

00:07:42.327 --> 00:07:44.430
or The Roots and I
went down to --

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.698
Me and The Roots, right?

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.867
Went down to Macy's
to rehearse our performance

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:50.469
in the Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.238
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it really fun.

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:55.474
Obviously socially distant,
safe and all of that.

00:07:55.474 --> 00:07:58.277
But we didn't know if we're
going to do a parade this year

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.179
or not or anything.
We actually didn't know.

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:02.414
But then we got the call
from NBC.

00:08:02.414 --> 00:08:05.217
They were like, "Hey, would you
like to be part of it?"

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:06.352
And how do you say no to that?

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.920
So we were like,
"Yeah, let's do it.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.188
We got to show up."

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:11.357
So I was like,
"Are we going to be on a float?"

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:13.993
'Cause usually we're on a muffin
or something.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.160
-[ Laughs ] Right.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.296
-We've been on guitar.

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:18.330
-Guitar.
-Yeah.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.732
-A muffin.

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:20.766
-"Sesame Street."

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.001
-Yeah, what was the
"Sesame Street"?

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.068
-Oh, yeah, "Sesame Street."

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:24.504
We were in, like, a house
with those guys.

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:27.139
-Yeah.
-Weren't we on a train before?

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.308
-I think the first year
we were on a train.

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:30.876
-Yeah.
-Yeah, we're on a train.

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:32.411
But so anyways,
I said, "What float?"

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:34.213
They said, "No float."
-Aw.

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:36.382
-You guys are dancing
in the street.

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:38.517
I go, "Alright, cool. I gotcha."

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:41.621
So we're going to be out there
on the street doing it up.

00:08:41.621 --> 00:08:44.890
It's going to be fun. It's all
going down Thanksgiving morning.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.660
We -- I asked around.
I found out how they're doing --

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.695
They're doing
some of the balloons, I think.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:53.532
I think they're just
going around Macy's,

00:08:53.532 --> 00:08:56.469
in and out
of the revolving door.

00:08:56.469 --> 00:08:58.304
-With the balloon.
-With the giant balloon, yeah.

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.839
They're just shoving it through.
They go, "What is that?"

00:09:00.839 --> 00:09:02.575
And they go, "Just trust me,
it's Snoopy.

00:09:02.575 --> 00:09:04.944
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:06.245
Just trust --
We couldn't blow it up.

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:09.548
But trust me, that's Snoopy
and that's --" Yeah.

00:09:09.548 --> 00:09:10.849
But, no,
they have some cool ideas.

00:09:10.849 --> 00:09:11.950
They are going to do
something different.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.619
It's just -- It's exciting

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:16.088
'cause you can't --
You can't not do the parade.

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:17.656
You got do the parade.
-Yeah.

00:09:17.656 --> 00:09:19.491
-Yeah. So it's going down,
and we'll be there.

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:21.293
They have all sorts
of fun performances.

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:23.228
I heard -- "Hamilton," I heard.

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:25.364
I heard "Mean Girls."

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:27.700
-Got to have your Rockettes.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.735
-I think that's
what going to, like...

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:32.738
[ Irish accent ]
...bring a tear to me eye,

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:33.973
is what they say.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.075
You know, it brings out
the Irish brogue."

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.176
-Yeah, man.
-You know?

00:09:38.176 --> 00:09:39.611
-And it bring --
-Mine, too.

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:41.079
-Yeah. And what --
What happens --

00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:43.382
What happens
when your Irish voice comes out?

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:45.651
What does it sound like there?
-I start to sound like Popeye.

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:46.985
I go, "Oh, ga, ga, ga, ga."

00:09:46.985 --> 00:09:48.687
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:50.456
He will not there
this year, Popeye.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:51.824
-Right.
-No, no, no.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:53.459
They'll wheel him out through
the revolving door.

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:56.161
[ Normal voice ] They go,
"That's Popeye. Trust me."

00:09:56.161 --> 00:09:57.162
But that's all going down.

00:09:57.162 --> 00:09:58.430
It was so exciting
to see everybody.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.831
Yeah, hopefully the Rockettes.

00:09:59.831 --> 00:10:02.067
That's going to be the one
that's going to be cool.

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:04.870
But obviously hosted
by Savannah,

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.339
I'm assuming Al, and Hoda.

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:08.774
But anyways,
the Thanksgiving Day Parade

